(6636678, 990082, 140026, '<td valign="top">The ''fake look'' via topaz making toys look like real life vehicles works well.  And the remnant shallow DOF because of the close range to subject gives it a ''tilt-shift'' effect thrown in also. <br/> <br/>I''ll bet it''s based on a real story that actually took place on a construction site?   <br/> <br/>The ''cartoon effect'' was probably the only direction to go in from images of toys. In the CGI film Ice Age 1, to portray the mammoth''s ''flash-back'' memory, they had to animate crude cave wall paintings. I think you''d done a similar thing here.<br/> <br/></td>', 'The ''fake look'' via topaz making toys look like real life vehicles works well.  And the remnant shallow DOF because of the close range to subject gives it a ''tilt-shift'' effect thrown in also.  I''ll bet it''s based on a real story that actually took place on a construction site?    The ''cartoon effect'' was probably the only direction to go in from images of toys. In the CGI film Ice Age 1, to portray the mammoth''s ''flash-back'' memory, they had to animate crude cave wall paintings. I think you''d done a similar thing here. ', '2012-01-06 10:19:08.000000', NULL, 0),
